          %p which satisfy certain evident axioms.
          %h3#as_a_generalized_multicategory As a generalized multicategory
          %p
            A cartesian multicategory can equivalently be defined as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+multicategory"} generalized multicategory
            relative to the monad on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            (or more precisely
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Prof"} Prof
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
          %h3#in_terms_of_the_action_of_a_faithful_cartesian_club In terms of the action of a faithful cartesian club
          %p
            An explicit elementary definition is perhaps most conveniently stated in terms of an action of the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/club"} club
            of functions”.
          %p
            A
            %em cartesian multicategory
            is a multicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            equipped with operations,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi σ
                      %mo )
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mo .
                      %mo .
                      %mo .
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi n
                      %mo ;
                      %mi B
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mi m
                  %mo ;
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi n
                  %mo ;
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(- \cdot \sigma\right)_{A_1, ..., A_n;B} : M(A_{\sigma 1}, ..., A_{\sigma m};B) \to M(A_{1}, ..., A_{n} ; B)
          %p
            for every function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma : \{1,...,m\} \to \{1, ..., n\}
            and objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo .
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1,...,A_n,B
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
